{"kind": "message", "turn": 8, "speaker": "Y", "content": "**storage.py** (draft):  \n```python\nimport json\nimport os\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom typing import List, Dict, Any\n\nEXPENSES_FILE = \"expenses.json\"\n\ndef load_expenses() -> List[Dict[str, Any]]:\n    \"\"\"Load expenses from JSON file. Returns empty list if file doesn't exist.\"\"\"\n    if not Path(EXPENSES_FILE).is_file():\n        return []\n    try:\n        with open(EXPENSES_FILE, \"r\") as f:\n            data = json.load(f)\n        # Validate schema\n        for entry in data:\n            assert \"date\" in entry and isinstance(entry[\"date\"], str)\n            assert \"category\" in entry and isinstance(entry[\"category\"], str)\n            assert \"amount\" in entry and isinstance(entry[\"amount\"], (int, float))\n            assert entry[\"amount\"] > 0\n            assert \"description\" in entry and isinstance(entry[\"description\"], str)\n        return data\n    except (json.JSONDecodeError, AssertionError, KeyError) as e:\n        raise ValueError(f\"Invalid expense data in {EXPENSES_FILE}: {e}\")\n\ndef save_expenses(expenses: List[Dict[str, Any]]) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Save expenses to JSON file.\"\"\"\n    try:\n        with open(EXPENSES_FILE, \"w\") as f:\n            json.dump(expenses, f, indent=2)\n    except Exception as e:\n        raise IOError(f\"Failed to save expenses: {e}\")\n```\n\n**Notes**:  \n- Uses `pathlib.Path` for robust file checks.  \n- Validates schema on load: required fields, type, positive amount.  \n- Raises clear errors for malformed data.  \n- `json.dump` with `indent=2` for readability.  \n\nNext: `commands.py` with `add_cmd`, `list_cmd`, etc., using `utils.py` for shared logic.", "eval_count": 391, "prompt_eval_count": 1857, "done_reason": "stop", "wall": 4.37}
